{
    "_note": "The photography manifest: one Unsplash photo id per image slot. `pnpm photos` downloads these, crops them to the slot's aspect ratio, writes the committed WebP files under public/img/, and regenerates content/credits.json from the live metadata so an attribution can never drift from the file it describes.",
    "_licence": "Unsplash's free licence permits commercial use and modification with no attribution required. We attribute anyway. The fetch script REFUSES an Unsplash+ (premium) photo, whose licence is different and is not free — that check is the reason the ids live here rather than being pasted into a shell command.",
    "_alt": "⚠️ SWAPPING A PHOTO MEANS REWRITING ITS ALT TEXT. Alt text lives in the translation catalogue (messages/*.json), not here — it is copy, and it is translated like the rest. Nothing links the two, so an id changed here leaves a sentence describing a photograph that is no longer on the page, which is worse than no alt text at all.",
    "_ratios": "Derived from the slot name, not stored per entry: `site/*` is 21:9, `*-hero` is 15:8, everything else is 3:2. One rule, so a new slot cannot be given a ratio the layout does not use.",
